            harvest_time_unparsed: "Ripens late September.",
            description: "University of Minnesota origin. Long stemmed, very large fruit with a red blush over a yellow background. The flesh is exceptionally crisp and juicy with a mild sweet flavor. The fruit remain crisp even after extended storage. The tree is moderately vigorous and upright; bears annually. Winter hardy. Ripens late September"
