            description: "Most popular apple in Wisconsin. Very good for fresh use, baking, and sauces; stores well. Fruit tends to drop prematurely. Annual bearing. Very susceptible to apple scab. Spur-type strains such as Macspur, Spur McIntosh, or Marshall McIntosh are similar and suitable. Ripens mid-September"
